Package: anon
Title: Redact and Pseudonymize Sensitive Data in R Objects
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Nash", "Delcamp", , "nash.delcamp@simulations-plus.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Applies anonymization techniques (redaction, recoding or pseudonymization, generalization, randomization and date shifting) to sensitive information in R objects including data frames, variable labels, lists, and character/factor/numeric vectors. Features pattern-based and NLP-based redaction, functions for common data types (identifiers, dates, emails, phone numbers, numeric values), and environment summaries with these techniques applied. Designed to help data scientists share code, results and context while protecting sensitive information. Applying these techniques does not by itself make data anonymous; that depends on the re-identification risk that remains.
URL: https://nash-delcamp-slp.github.io/anon/, https://github.com/nash-delcamp-slp/anon
